      "writtenOn": "2026-07-22T14:23:34Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Thanks @pbdr@google.com for the context of planned fix. \n\nThe config overlay approach sounds good to us. Should we look at implementing config_external_display_enable_on_connect from our side in the framework, or will this be handled from the AOSP side?\n\nAlso, a couple of quick clarifications before we proceed:\n\u003e 1 ) When this overlay is set to true, should shouldAutoEnable return true and skip the setEnabledLocked(false) call entirely? That is the key part for us the disable → re-enable cycle is what triggers the re-init sequence causing no layers.\n\n\u003e 2 ) Should this work on user builds without any IS_ENG || IS_USERDEBUG condition?",
      "parentUuid": "badbd1a7_96b88bca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 288,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 288,
        "endChar": 48
